<Base title="Our story" description="The thinking behind I Will Bloom, founded by Rachel to make space for the emotional side of cancer."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / There is a person behind every appointment.</nav><p class="eyebrow">Our story · Rachel, founder</p><h1>There is a person behind every appointment.</h1><p>I Will Bloom grew from Rachel’s experience of cancer and the recognition that practical schedules are only one part of what someone carries through treatment.</p><p>There are thoughts that arrive after an appointment. Questions that have nothing to do with medicine. Ordinary things you still want to notice. Feelings that do not fit neatly into a conversation.</p><h2>Support for your mind — not just your schedule.</h2><p>The journal brings guided reflection, gentle activities and practical space together. It offers somewhere to begin when a blank page feels difficult, and permission to use that space in your own way.</p><h2>No pressure to be positive</h2><p>You do not have to turn a hard day into a lesson. Hope, anger, relief, boredom and uncertainty can all belong on the same page.</p><p>That is the heart of I Will Bloom: making room for your experience, without deciding how it should look.</p><p><a class="btn ghost" href="/the-purpose/">Meet the journal →</a></p><p class="smallnote">Founder-story draft for Rachel’s final review. The original founder letter will be preserved once its current text is verified.</p></article></Base>